    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test green).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Points system** replacing the old level rules. The membership level is now derived from a points total rather than computed directly.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 The DTOs are OpenAPI-generated at build time, so the contract lives here. Added a new `membershipPoints` field (`minimum: 0`) and widened `membershipLevel` to `1\u20134`, updating both descriptions to document the new rules.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n   - Added a `membershipPoints(owner)` method: starts at 0, `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+, `+3` for tenure over 365 days (reusing the existing `hasQualifyingTenure` helper).\n   - Rewrote `membershipLevel(owner)` to derive from points: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n   - Added the `membershipPoints` mapping to `toOwnerDto` so **both fields are returned**.\n\nNull handling is preserved (both return `null` for a `null` owner). The acceptance test's scenario \u2014 fresh owner with email (+2) and no namesake (+1), single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2 \u2014 passes.",
